+## Fork imported history
+
+A saved transcript has imported message IDs such as `seed_message_2`, separate from execution turn IDs. To replace an imported user message, create a new conversation with a first message and this fork reference:
+
+```json
+{
+  "message": "Replacement question",
+  "operationId": "replacement-operation",
+  "fork": {
+    "sessionId": "owned-source-session",
+    "beforeMessageId": "seed_message_2"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The channel must grant source access through `authorizeFork`; anonymous callers cannot fork. `beforeMessageId` selects an existing imported user message and excludes it and everything after it. Do not combine it with `beforeTurnId` or `checkpointId`. Forking the first imported user message starts with empty history.
+
+The new session retains its own authentication, instructions, limits, and execution identity. eve derives model and display history from the same durable imported prefix. Completed tool results remain historical content; tools are not replayed. Imported attachments are resolved through the destination channel on the first turn. A later source sandbox is not inherited. Application-owned documents must be restored separately to the selected boundary. Imported messages retained in the prefix remain addressable in descendant forks.
+
+Imported assistant seed messages may include an optional `modelId` (1–512 characters), using the same provider/model reference as `step.started`. It is preserved in display metadata across imported forks. This informational value does not select a model or change executable history; the application chooses the model for a new turn. User seed messages and arbitrary metadata remain rejected.
